  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bosnia and Herzegovina: Strengthening Local Capacities for Disaster Preparedness and Response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">While an upper-middle-income country, Bosnia and Herzegovina (BiH) has both systemic and immediate needs for Disaster Risk Reduction (DRR) initiatives. BiH is still grappling with the aftermath of the war, a fragmented governance structure, weak institutions, and is at an increasing risk of disasters due to climate change and environmental degradation. Climate change projections for BiH predict increases in natural disasters&apos; frequency, unpredictability and intensity, which could exacerbate existing political and social tensions. The floods of 2014 can serve as a warning sign for future events. In 2014 the country experienced devastating floods that affected one in four inhabitants and resulted in significant economic losses. BiH is also at risk of other disasters, most prominently landslides, heatwaves, forest fires, and earthquakes.This project will support BiH EU accession process, as well as national priorities and international commitments on DRR, while focusing on a people-centred approach to improving the safety, security, and well-being of people in hazard-prone areas, with a focus on the most vulnerable groups. As such, the overall objective of the proposed intervention is to contribute to strengthening the preparedness and response to hazardous events of local communities and disaster response actors at the local, entity, and state levels in Bosnia and Herzegovina.This project will be closely coordinated with the Ministry of Security (MoS) at the national level, entity, and district level civil protection authorities, organizations, and groups. Additionally, at the local level IOM will seek out the participation of local community leaders, both men, and women, as key for the successful engagement with local communities. Specifically, IOM will work with the Civil Protection Directorate of RS, the Civil Protection Directorate of the FBiH, Brcko District Public Security Department, the BiH Red Cross, the Red Cross of RS, the Red Cross of the FBiH, and the Red Cross of Brcko District, local level Red Cross societies, first responders and other volunteer and professional civil protection organizations.</narrative>
  </description>
